## Parent
- Spec: benchmark-gepa-overhaul
- Goals: G-1, G-3
- Depends on: bench-result-substrate
- Frozen decisions: F-1

## Problem

Parent goal: Grow the benchmark with FeatureBench, the Gin render-context task, and a few cherry-picked tasks, in a format GEPA can optimize against once-run stored baselines, with a model judge for structural-tool applicability.

This curd ships G-1 (FeatureBench tasks run in our harness) and the external half of G-3 (one Go and one Rust SWE-bench Multilingual instance beside the three local hard tasks), under F-1 (fully native, no Docker). Citations are at HEAD `806ea7b`, where bench-result-substrate has landed. Today the harness can only run tasks whose repository is a pinned fixture:

- `run_single` copies `get_repo_path(task.repo)` (`benchmark/run.py:162-166`) through `_agent_repo` (`benchmark/run.py:353-400`).
- Cell identity, both runner lanes, and the main loop look the task up in the static `TASKS` dict (`benchmark/run.py:648,704,743,1566`, `benchmark/tasks/__init__.py:80-147`), and cells are planned with their identity before any runs (`benchmark/run.py:1462-1470`).
- `main` exits when a task repo is not cloned under `REPOS` (`benchmark/run.py:1424-1433`) and cleans every selected repo before and after the run (`benchmark/run.py:1435-1438,1725-1728`).
- `Task.source` indexes `REPOS` for every non-synthetic task (`benchmark/tasks/base.py:84-93`).
- `cell_identity` takes `env_fingerprint(task.repo)`, which resolves `get_repo_path` and so `REPOS[repo_name]` (`benchmark/run.py:532-542,665`). `_cell_task_digest` hashes prompt, ground truth, test command, fixture files, the `REPOS` commit, and task sources (`benchmark/run.py:621-633`), none of which would carry an external instance's patches, test lists, `base_commit`, or data revision.
- Every cell gets the constant 600 s timeout `CELL_TIMEOUT_S` (`benchmark/run.py:497`) in the streaming kill timer, its `TimeoutExpired`, the non-streaming subprocess timeout, and the timeout message (`benchmark/run.py:915,934,949,1687`). `cell_identity` hashes that same constant into the run key (`benchmark/run.py:667`). That is too short for a Rust compile plus an agent fix.

Grading is required strings or one `test_command` (`benchmark/tasks/base.py:143-186`). The only held-out-test grader is the bespoke Gin task (`benchmark/tasks/gin_render_context_tasks.py:116-167`), whose held-out tests sit inside the tilth `benchmark/` tree (`benchmark/tasks/gin_render_context_tasks.py:17`) and whose failure reason carries held-out test output (`benchmark/tasks/gin_render_context_tasks.py:155-156`). The row carries only `correct` and `correctness_reason` from grading (`benchmark/run.py:1018-1023,1083-1084`). Nothing detects an agent that reads the benchmark tree, where local ground truth lives, or that fetches the upstream fix; tilth trusts absolute paths and Bash can read anywhere.

## Contract

The external task adapter (parent curd c2) changes only the benchmark harness.

- **Task hooks.** `run.py` honors four optional task hooks, used only when present (F-1):
  - `prepare(workdir)`: when a task defines it, `run_single` creates a fresh temporary workdir and calls the hook instead of copying a `REPOS` fixture through `_agent_repo`, and `main` skips `REPOS` validation and cleaning for that task. Tasks without the hook keep today's `_agent_repo` path unchanged.
  - `grade_details()`: called after `check_correctness`; its dict is merged into the row.
  - `identity_inputs() -> Mapping[str, object]`: when present, `run._cell_task_digest` passes it to `baselines.task_digest` as an added input, so it enters the task digest and the run key.
  - `timeout_s`: an optional task attribute, default `CELL_TIMEOUT_S` (600). c2 changes `run.py` to use the task's value in the streaming kill timer and its `TimeoutExpired` (`benchmark/run.py:915,934`), in the non-streaming subprocess timeout (`benchmark/run.py:949`), in the timeout message (`benchmark/run.py:1687`), and in `cell_identity`'s `timeout_s` (`benchmark/run.py:667`). The row and the run key therefore record the timeout the cell actually ran under. External Go and Rust tasks set 1800 and FeatureBench Python tasks set 1200 [AGENT-DECIDED; alternative one global `--timeout` flag].
- **Harness data directory.** Dataset rows, upstream mirrors, gold patches, held-out tests, FAIL_TO_PASS and PASS_TO_PASS lists, and admission verdicts live only in `$TILTH_BENCH_DATA` (default `~/.local/share/tilth-bench/external`) [AGENT-DECIDED; alternative `/tmp/tilth_bench/external` beside the fixture repos]. It lies outside the tilth checkout and every workdir.
- **Dataset rows.** Rows are cached as fetched, with their real keys and no added fields:
  - FeatureBench Lite v1.1 (HF tag `v1.1`, `data/lite-00000-of-00001.parquet`): `instance_id`, `patch`, `test_patch`, `FAIL_TO_PASS`, `PASS_TO_PASS`, `image_name`, `repo`, `base_commit`, `problem_statement`, `repo_settings`. The row `patch` is the mask: it applies forward to `base_commit` and removes the feature implementation. `test_patch` is a deleted-file diff of the FAIL_TO_PASS test files and also applies forward. FAIL_TO_PASS and PASS_TO_PASS entries are test file paths. The level is the `instance_id` suffix (`.lv1` or `.lv2`). Rows carry no hardware field.
  - SWE-bench Multilingual at HF revision `846e647b`: its dataset columns, including `instance_id`, `repo`, `base_commit`, `patch` (the gold fix), `test_patch` (the held-out tests), `problem_statement`, `FAIL_TO_PASS`, `PASS_TO_PASS`, and `eval_script`. It has no `language` column. FAIL_TO_PASS and PASS_TO_PASS entries are test IDs. No level or hardware filter applies.
- **Loading (G-1, G-3).** `external.featurebench.load(instance_id, data_rev)` and `external.swebench_ml.load(instance_id, data_rev)` build an `ExternalTask` from the cached row at the pinned revision. A load at any other revision raises.
  - The task's `name` is the instance ID, its `repo` is the dataset name (`featurebench` or `swebench_ml`) [AGENT-DECIDED; alternative the upstream `owner/repo` slug], its `source` names the upstream URL and `base_commit` without indexing `REPOS`, and its `prompt` is the problem statement alone.
  - `ExternalTask` exposes `problem_statement: str` (the row's `problem_statement`) and `gold_patch: str`, the diff that adds the fix. For SWE-bench Multilingual that is the row `patch`. For FeatureBench it is the reverse of the row `patch`. The parent model judge (c4) labels external tasks from these two.
  - `external.cached_row(instance_id: str) -> Mapping | None` is a read-only accessor: it returns the full cached row, with its real keys, for an instance of either pinned dataset at its pinned revision, and `None` when that row has not been fetched. It never fetches, writes, or starts a subprocess. The panel curd (c3) uses it as `load_panel`'s default row source.
  - `external.language_of(row: Mapping) -> str` is a pure function. It returns the row's `language` column when present, else the language its `repo` maps to in the pinned candidate repository map (every FeatureBench repository maps to `python`). For a row without a `language` column whose `repo` is outside the map, it raises `ValueError` [AGENT-DECIDED; alternative return `unknown`]. It reads only `repo` and `language`, so it works on the redacted rows c3 commits (`instance_id`, `repo`, `base_commit`). `ExternalTask.language` equals `language_of(row)` and is one of `python`, `go`, or `rust`.
  - `external.resolve_task(name) -> Task | None` looks the name up as an instance ID in the cached rows of both pinned datasets, calls `external.preflight.admit(name)`, and returns the `ExternalTask` only when the verdict is admitted, else `None`; an unknown name returns `None` without calling `admit`. `run.py --tasks` and the judge resolver (c4) use it. For a `--tasks` name not in `TASKS`, `run.py` calls `resolve_task` before planning, registers the result in the process `TASKS` dict under that name, so `cell_identity` and the lookups at `benchmark/run.py:648,704,743,1566` find it, and runs it through `prepare`. `--tasks all` keeps meaning the local registry only [AGENT-DECIDED; alternative a separate `--external` flag].
  - The FeatureBench candidate set is the parent's curated Pareto-12 CPU subset: the COSPA `featurebench_lite_pareto12_v1.json` instance list restricted to `.lv1` IDs, minus the parent-deferred heavy-environment repositories (pandas, astropy, transformers, Lightning, mlflow). CPU-only is enforced by that curated list plus the admission round trip on a CPU host. `repo_settings.docker_specs.run_args.cuda_visible_devices` is never read as a GPU signal, because CPU-only Pareto-12 rows set it.
  - The SWE-bench Multilingual cherry picks are Go `gin-gonic__gin-3741` with fallback `prometheus__prometheus-14861`, and Rust `sharkdp__bat-2650` with fallback `tokio-rs__tokio-6724`.
- **Prepared workspace (F-1).** `ExternalTask.prepare(workdir)`:
  - exports the `base_commit` tree from the upstream mirror with `git archive`;
  - for FeatureBench, applies the row `patch` forward, which masks the implementation, and then applies `test_patch` forward, which deletes the FAIL_TO_PASS test files, so the agent never sees held-out tests. The method `mask_patch_forward` is recorded in the task's `source.transformation`, which already lands in every row's `source`, and in the admission verdict `reason`. SWE-bench Multilingual applies neither patch;
  - commits the result as the single commit of a fresh `git init` repository with no upstream history and no remote;
  - writes no gold patch, test patch, held-out test file, or FAIL_TO_PASS/PASS_TO_PASS list into the workdir.
- **Native environment (F-1).** Python instances get a `uv` venv at `<workdir>/.venv` built from the row's `repo_settings` install steps, reusing the uv cache [AGENT-DECIDED; alternative a shared per-instance venv outside both trees] [speculating: those install steps translate to `uv`; the admission round trip proves it per task]. Go and Rust instances use the host toolchain and fetch modules or crates with `go mod download` or `cargo fetch` at prepare time. `.venv/` and `target/` go into `.git/info/exclude`. No code path in loading, preparing, admitting, or grading starts `docker` or `podman`.
- **Identity.** An `ExternalTask`'s `identity_inputs()` returns its gold patch, `test_patch`, FAIL_TO_PASS, PASS_TO_PASS, `base_commit`, and data revision. For a task that exposes `language`, `run.env_fingerprint` probes that language's toolchains (`uv` and Python, `go`, or `rustc` and `cargo`). For a task with `prepare`, it hashes the lockfiles of the task's `base_commit` tree in the mirror instead of resolving `get_repo_path(task.repo)`, so it never indexes `REPOS`. This builds on the in-flight bench-result-substrate change that probes only the task language's toolchains plus `uv` for Python. A change in any one of these inputs changes the run key from `run.cell_identity`.
- **Native grading (F-1).** `ExternalTask.check_correctness(result_text, repo_path)`:
  1. extracts the agent's changes against the prepared commit, ignoring excluded paths;
  2. copies them onto a clean prepared checkout in a temporary directory;
  3. restores the held-out tests:
     - for FeatureBench, it resets every FAIL_TO_PASS and PASS_TO_PASS file to its `base_commit` content from the mirror, which brings back the FAIL_TO_PASS files that `test_patch` deleted, and does not apply `test_patch`;
     - for SWE-bench Multilingual, it resets every file `test_patch` touches to its `base_commit` content and then applies `test_patch`, as the row's `eval_script` does;
     - so in both datasets agent edits to the graded test files do not count;
  4. runs the FAIL_TO_PASS and PASS_TO_PASS tests natively and matches results per dataset:
     - FeatureBench entries are test file paths. The command runs pytest with `-rA` on those files inside the venv, with any test options from `repo_settings` [speculating: this derivation matches FeatureBench grading; the admission round trip proves it per task]. A listed file passes when pytest collects at least one test node whose ID starts with `<path>::` and every such node passes.
     - SWE-bench Multilingual entries are test IDs. The command is the test command line of the row's `eval_script` [speculating: it extracts cleanly; the admission round trip proves it per task]. Each ID must match exactly one verdict parsed from `go test -v` or `cargo test` output, or pytest `-rA` output for a Python instance.
     - A listed entry with no matching result counts as failed.
  - `correct` is true only when every listed entry passes. `grade_details()` returns only `pass_rate` (passed entries over FAIL_TO_PASS plus PASS_TO_PASS entries) [AGENT-DECIDED; alternative FAIL_TO_PASS only], `f2p_passed`, `f2p_total`, `p2p_passed`, and `p2p_total`, all counted in entries.
- **Grader-side material.** The external `correctness_reason` may carry held-out test output, as the Gin grader already does; it is grader-side material that the parent strips before any optimizer-side model sees a row. No other row field this curd adds carries a gold patch, held-out test source, or held-out test output. Agent-produced text, including the tool inputs quoted in `contamination_hits`, is kept verbatim.
- **Admission (F-1, G-1, G-3).** `external.preflight.admit(instance_id)` returns a `PreflightVerdict` exposing `admitted: bool` and `reason: str`.
  - For FeatureBench it refuses an `instance_id` ending `.lv2` (`level2`) or carrying no `.lv1` or `.lv2` suffix (`unclassified`). For any instance it refuses a failed environment build (`env_build_failed`) or a failed prepare step (`prepare_failed`). SWE-bench Multilingual has no level filter.
  - It then runs a round trip through `prepare` and `check_correctness` on this host. The gold patch (`gold_patch`, applied on the prepared tree) must resolve. The empty patch and the tampered patch must not (`gold_unresolved`, `empty_resolved`, `tampered_resolved`). The tampered patch is the gold patch minus its last source hunk, or, for a single-hunk gold patch, minus that hunk's added lines [AGENT-DECIDED; alternative gold plus deletion of the first added function body]. A passing round trip yields `reason: admitted` for SWE-bench Multilingual and `reason: admitted:mask_patch_forward` for FeatureBench.
  - This curd owns the verdict cache: each verdict is persisted in the harness data directory keyed by instance ID, data revision, and env fingerprint. When a cached verdict matches the key, `admit` returns it without re-running the admission round trip; computing the current env fingerprint may run version probes such as `go version`, `rustc --version`, or `uv --version`. The panel curd (c3) only reads verdicts through `admit`. Admission makes no model call and needs no `--max-usd`.
  - `run.py` guards external cells by calling `external.preflight.admit(instance_id)` for every planned external cell before any model call, so stubbing `admit` covers the guard. A non-admitted verdict exits the run naming the instance and its reason. When no verdict is cached under the current env fingerprint, that call runs the round trip first.
- **Preflight CLI (G-1, G-3).** `python3 benchmark/external/preflight.py` has two forms. Each prints every verdict with its gold, empty, and tampered pass counts.
  - No arguments: it admits the FeatureBench candidate set and, per language, the primary SWE-bench Multilingual pick, then the fallback only when the primary is refused. It prints a summary with `featurebench_admitted`, `go_admitted`, and `rust_admitted`. When any of the three is 0, it names that family and exits nonzero; parent AC-1 then refuses the panel rather than passing vacuously.
  - `--panel PATH`: it reads the panel JSON's `members` and admits exactly the members whose `family` is `featurebench` or `swebench_ml`, by their `id`, skipping local members and trying no fallback. It exits nonzero, naming each refused member, when any external member is refused or no FeatureBench member is admitted. This is the form the parent quality gate runs. It reads only `members[].id` and `members[].family` and does not call the panel loader [AGENT-DECIDED; alternative call `panels.load_panel`, which would make c2 depend on c3].
- **Contamination (F-1).** This curd guarantees only the `contaminated` field: every row `run.py` writes, local or external, carries `contaminated` as a bool and is never written without it. Applying the flag belongs to its consumers: the evolution loop (c5) scores a contaminated rollout incorrect and excludes it from reflection inside evolve, and the panel curd (c3) owns how `analyze.py` treats contaminated panel rows.
  - For a row with a trajectory sidecar, including a failure row that `record_failure` gives one (`benchmark/run.py:1544-1560`), `run.py` calls `external.contamination.scan(sidecar_path, task)` over the tool-call inputs in the sidecar [AGENT-DECIDED: inputs only; alternative also scan tool outputs].
  - A hit is an input that names a path under the tilth `benchmark/` tree (`config.BENCHMARK_DIR` resolved, after `~`, `$HOME`, and `..` normalization) or under the harness data directory; or that fetches the task's upstream repository (a `git clone` or `git fetch` of it, or a URL on its GitHub repository, codeload, or raw host) or the task's own package source (`pip download`, `uv pip download`, or an index install of the package name, a PyPI files URL, a crates.io download, or `go get` or `go mod download` of the module path). A local task's upstream is its `REPOS` URL; synthetic tasks have none.
  - c2 never changes `correct`: every row keeps the grader verdict there. A row with any hit records `contaminated: true` and `contamination_hits`; a row with no hit records `contaminated: false` [AGENT-DECIDED; alternative override `correct` on panel runs only].
  - A row with no sidecar to scan (an OpenCode cell, or a failure row whose `trajectory_path` is null) records `contaminated: true` with an `unscanned` hit, so no consumer treats an unverifiable rollout as clean; panel arms always have sidecars [AGENT-DECIDED; alternative `contaminated: false` plus a separate `contamination_scanned: false` field].
  - A stored row reused at `benchmark/run.py:1577-1582` that lacks the field is scanned from its stored `trajectory_path` before it is written.
- **Fixtures.** The work starts by committing synthetic instances under `benchmark/tests/fixtures/external/` whose rows use exactly the real row keys above and no level, hardware, or language fields:
  - a SWE-bench-shaped Python instance (stdlib-only project in a local bare repository, test-ID entries, `patch` adding the fix, `test_patch` adding tests) and Go and Rust variants;
  - a FeatureBench-shaped instance built like the real rows: an `.lv1` `instance_id`; a `base_commit` holding the feature and its FAIL_TO_PASS test file; a `patch` that applies forward and removes the implementation; a `test_patch` that is a deleted-file diff of the FAIL_TO_PASS file; file-path entries; and a `repo_settings`. It has an `.lv2` copy;
  - canned `go test -v`, `cargo test`, and pytest `-rA` outputs.
  - Tests make no network or model call.

## Grounding

| Probe | Outcome | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| wiki | hit | `.hallouminate/wiki/benchmark-harness-gotchas.md:85-88`: the Gin grader copies candidate source into a clean pinned fixture, restores original assertions, injects held-out tests after inference, and its preflight accepts the reference and rejects negative controls |
| explorer | hit | Explorer digest at HEAD `806ea7b`. Workspaces only from `REPOS` fixtures via `get_repo_path` and `_agent_repo` (`benchmark/run.py:162-166,353-400`). `TASKS` lookups in `cell_identity`, the runners, and the loop (`run.py:648,704,743,1566`), with identity computed at planning (`run.py:1462-1470`). `env_fingerprint` resolves `REPOS` through `get_repo_path` (`run.py:532-542`). `_cell_task_digest` inputs (`run.py:621-633`). Constant timeout at `run.py:497`, used at `run.py:667,915,934,949,1687`. `REPOS` validation and cleaning (`run.py:1424-1438,1725-1728`). Grading call at `run.py:1018-1023`, row at `run.py:1038-1096`, failure rows with sidecars at `run.py:1544-1560,1660-1723`, reused rows at `run.py:1577-1582`. `Task.source` (`benchmark/tasks/base.py:84-93`), registry (`benchmark/tasks/__init__.py:80-147`), `--tasks all` (`run.py:1120-1123,1341`). Gin held-out grader at `gin_render_context_tasks.py:116-167`, tests under `benchmark/` (`:17`), negative-control preflight at `gin_render_context_fixtures/preflight.py:38-60`. Research `benchmark-subscription-harness-auth.md` claims 11 and 16 to 19. r0 and r1 reviews of the real FeatureBench v1.1 Lite parquet and SWE-bench Multilingual `846e647b` rows: row keys; `.lv1`/`.lv2` suffixes; file-path F2P/P2P entries; no level, hardware, or language field; FeatureBench `patch` applies forward to `base_commit` and removes the implementation (sympy, sphinx, metaflow, seaborn x2, pydantic, xarray); `test_patch` is a deleted-file diff of the FAIL_TO_PASS file |

## Approach

1. **Fixtures first (F-1, G-1, G-3).** Commit the real-key synthetic instances, the FeatureBench instance built like the real rows (forward mask `patch`, deleted-file `test_patch`), its `.lv2` copy, and the canned Go, Rust, and pytest outputs under `benchmark/tests/fixtures/external/`.
2. **Hooks in run.py (F-1, G-1, G-3).**
   - `run_single` calls `task.prepare(workdir)` in a fresh temporary workdir when the hook exists, else `_agent_repo` as today.
   - `main` skips `REPOS` validation and cleaning for tasks with the hook. Before planning, it resolves a `--tasks` name outside `TASKS` through `external.resolve_task` and registers it in `TASKS`. It guards every planned external cell with `external.preflight.admit` before any model call.
   - The runner timers, the timeout message, and `cell_identity` take the task's `timeout_s` (default `CELL_TIMEOUT_S`).
   - `_cell_task_digest` adds `identity_inputs()`, and `env_fingerprint` keys on `task.language` and the `base_commit` lockfiles for prepared tasks.
   - The row builder merges `grade_details()`.
3. **Loaders and prepare (F-1, G-1, G-3).** New `benchmark/external/` package:
   - `ExternalTask(Task)` with `problem_statement`, `gold_patch` (reverse of the FeatureBench `patch`), `language`, and `identity_inputs()`;
   - `cached_row`, `language_of`, `featurebench.load`, `swebench_ml.load`, and `resolve_task`;
   - a fetch step that caches rows and upstream mirrors in the harness data directory;
   - `prepare`, with `git archive` export, FeatureBench forward `patch` then forward `test_patch` (`mask_patch_forward`), and a fresh `git init`;
   - per-task `timeout_s` (1800 Go and Rust, 1200 FeatureBench) and the native env build (`uv` venv, host Go or Rust toolchain).
4. **Native grader (F-1, G-1, G-3).** `check_correctness` follows the Gin held-out pattern: it copies agent changes onto a clean prepared copy, restores the FeatureBench FAIL_TO_PASS and PASS_TO_PASS files from `base_commit` without `test_patch` (SWE-bench resets and applies `test_patch`), and runs the tests. FeatureBench uses file-level pytest aggregation and SWE-bench Multilingual uses exact test-ID matching. `grade_details()` returns entry counts only.
5. **Admission (F-1, G-1, G-3).** `preflight.admit` has the `.lv1`/`.lv2` suffix filter, the gold (reverse `patch` for FeatureBench), empty, and tampered round trip, and the verdict cache this curd owns. The preflight CLI has a no-argument form (candidates, Go and Rust fallback, per-family counts) and a `--panel PATH` form (exactly the panel's external members). If zero FeatureBench tasks are admitted, the CLI reports it and exits nonzero, and parent AC-1 refuses the panel; G-1 then returns to the user.
6. **Contamination scan (F-1, G-1, G-3).** `contamination.scan` runs over sidecar tool inputs for every row with a sidecar, local tasks and failure rows included. Every written row, including reused rows, gets `contaminated`, plus `contamination_hits`. `correct` keeps the grader verdict; c5 and c3 apply the flag.

## Interface sketches

```text
slice:            benchmark (existing harness) + NEW SLICE benchmark/external/
spine step:       workflow (run.py cell loop) + infra (native checkout and env builder)
public interface: Task.prepare(workdir) and Task.grade_details() optional hooks, called by run.py when present  (c2, F-1)
detail:           Task.identity_inputs() -> Mapping[str, object] optional hook, added to run._cell_task_digest; Task.timeout_s optional attribute, default CELL_TIMEOUT_S 600, used by the runner timers, the timeout message, and run.cell_identity timeout_s; ExternalTask sets 1800 (Go, Rust) or 1200 (FeatureBench)  (G-1, G-3, F-1)
public interface: external.ExternalTask(Task); external.featurebench.load / external.swebench_ml.load -> ExternalTask; external.preflight.admit(instance_id) -> PreflightVerdict; external.contamination.scan(sidecar_path, task) -> bool  (c2, F-1)
detail:           ExternalTask.problem_statement: str; ExternalTask.gold_patch: str, the fix diff (SWE-bench row patch; FeatureBench reverse of row patch) (read by c4); ExternalTask.language in {python, go, rust}  (G-1, G-3)
public interface: external.cached_row(instance_id: str) -> Mapping | None; read-only; the full cached row of either pinned dataset, None when not fetched; no fetch, write, or subprocess (c3 load_panel default row source)  (G-1, G-3, F-1)
public interface: external.language_of(row: Mapping) -> str; pure; row language column, else the pinned repo map; reads only repo and language, so it works on c3's redacted rows  (G-1, G-3, F-1)
detail:           featurebench.load(instance_id, data_rev) / swebench_ml.load(instance_id, data_rev)  (G-1, G-3, F-1)
public interface: external.resolve_task(name) -> Task | None; the ExternalTask for a cached-row instance ID whose admit verdict is admitted, else None (used by run.py --tasks and c4)  (G-1, G-3, F-1)
detail:           PreflightVerdict.admitted: bool; PreflightVerdict.reason: str (admitted, admitted:mask_patch_forward, level2, unclassified, env_build_failed, prepare_failed, gold_unresolved, empty_resolved, tampered_resolved); plus instance_id, dataset, data_rev, env_fingerprint, gold/empty/tampered pass counts; verdicts cached by c2, read by c3 and by the run.py guard through admit  (G-1, G-3, F-1)
public interface: row field contaminated: bool on every row run.py writes, with correct left as the grader verdict (applied by c5 in evolve; panel-row analyze handling owned by c3)  (F-1, G-1, G-3)
public interface: python3 benchmark/external/preflight.py [--panel PATH]; no-arg form prints featurebench_admitted, go_admitted, rust_admitted and exits nonzero when any is 0; --panel form admits exactly the panel external members and exits nonzero when any is refused or none is FeatureBench  (G-1, G-3, F-1)
private:          harness data directory layout, row and mirror fetch, git archive export, forward mask and test_patch application, reverse-patch gold builder, uv venv and Go/Rust env builders, base_commit lockfile hashing, test-command derivation, per-dataset result matching and output parsers, tampered-patch builder, verdict cache format, pinned repo-to-language map, scan patterns and path normalization
crust delta:      new row fields pass_rate, f2p_passed, f2p_total, p2p_passed, p2p_total, contaminated, contamination_hits; row timeout_s now the task timeout; new Task.timeout_s and Task.identity_inputs hooks; baselines.task_digest takes identity_inputs; FeatureBench source.transformation records mask_patch_forward; new package benchmark/external/; run.py --tasks accepts admitted instance IDs  (G-1, G-3, F-1)
arrows:           run.py -> external, baselines; external -> tasks.base, config; no arrow from external into run.py or panels; no arrow from tilth src/ into benchmark/
```

## Acceptance
- AC-1: WHEN `run.py` runs a cell for a task that defines `prepare` THE SYSTEM SHALL call `prepare(workdir)` in a fresh temporary workdir instead of copying a `REPOS` fixture and SHALL skip `REPOS` validation and cleaning for that task, and WHEN the task is an `ExternalTask` the workdir SHALL hold the `base_commit` tree in a fresh `git init` repository whose only commit is that tree, with no upstream history or remote, FeatureBench rows SHALL have the row `patch` and then `test_patch` applied forward, so the implementation and the FAIL_TO_PASS test files are absent, with `mask_patch_forward` recorded in `source.transformation`, and the workdir SHALL contain no gold patch, test patch, held-out test file, or FAIL_TO_PASS/PASS_TO_PASS list; WHEN a task defines no `prepare` THE SYSTEM SHALL use the existing `_agent_repo` path; WHEN `run.py` plans or runs a cell THE SYSTEM SHALL use the task's `timeout_s`, `CELL_TIMEOUT_S` when the task sets none, in the runner timers, the timeout message, and `cell_identity`'s `timeout_s` and run key.  (F-1, G-1, G-3)
- AC-2: WHEN `prepare` builds an external task environment THE SYSTEM SHALL create a `uv` venv in the workdir for Python instances and use the host Go or Rust toolchain for Go and Rust instances, SHALL start no `docker` or `podman` process while loading, preparing, admitting, or grading, and WHEN `run.cell_identity` computes the identity of a loaded `ExternalTask` THE SYSTEM SHALL not index `REPOS`, SHALL include its `identity_inputs()` in the task digest, SHALL key its env fingerprint on `task.language` and the `base_commit` lockfiles, and SHALL compute a different run key when any one of the gold patch, `test_patch`, FAIL_TO_PASS, PASS_TO_PASS, `base_commit`, the data revision, the toolchain version, or the lockfile hash changes.  (F-1, G-1, G-3)
- AC-3: WHEN an external task cell finishes THE SYSTEM SHALL copy the agent's changes, without excluded paths, onto a clean prepared checkout; for FeatureBench SHALL restore every FAIL_TO_PASS and PASS_TO_PASS file from `base_commit` without applying `test_patch`, and for SWE-bench Multilingual SHALL reset the files `test_patch` touches and apply it; SHALL run the FAIL_TO_PASS and PASS_TO_PASS tests natively; SHALL count a FeatureBench file entry passed only when pytest collected at least one `<path>::` node from it and all of them passed, count a SWE-bench Multilingual entry passed only on an exact test-ID match that passed, and count an unmatched entry failed; SHALL return `correct` true from `check_correctness` only when every entry passes; and SHALL merge `pass_rate`, `f2p_passed`, `f2p_total`, `p2p_passed`, and `p2p_total` from `grade_details()` into the row, with no gold patch or held-out test source or output in any field other than `correctness_reason`.  (F-1, G-1, G-3)
- AC-4: WHEN `external.preflight.admit` runs THE SYSTEM SHALL return a `PreflightVerdict` with `admitted` and `reason`, admitting an instance only when, on this host, its `gold_patch` resolves on the prepared tree and its empty and tampered patches do not through `prepare` and `check_correctness`, with FeatureBench reason `admitted:mask_patch_forward`; SHALL refuse a FeatureBench `.lv2` or suffixless `instance_id` and any instance whose environment build or prepare step fails with a named reason; SHALL apply no level filter to SWE-bench Multilingual; SHALL make no model call; and SHALL cache the verdict keyed by instance ID, data revision, and env fingerprint; WHEN a cached verdict matches that key THE SYSTEM SHALL return it without re-running the admission round trip, including from a fresh process; WHEN `run.py` plans an external cell THE SYSTEM SHALL obtain its verdict through `external.preflight.admit` and, when it is not admitted, exit before any model call naming the instance and reason.  (F-1, G-1, G-3)
- AC-5: WHEN `featurebench.load` or `swebench_ml.load` is called THE SYSTEM SHALL build, from the row cached in the harness data directory at the pinned revision, an `ExternalTask` named by the instance ID, with `repo` set to the dataset name, a `source` that does not index `REPOS`, the problem statement alone as the prompt, `problem_statement` equal to the row text, `gold_patch` equal to the row `patch` for SWE-bench Multilingual and to its reverse for FeatureBench, and `language` equal to `external.language_of(row)`, and SHALL raise for any other revision; WHEN `external.cached_row` gets an instance ID THE SYSTEM SHALL return the full cached row with its real keys when it has been fetched, else `None`, without fetching, writing, or starting a subprocess; WHEN `external.language_of` gets a row THE SYSTEM SHALL return its `language` column when present, else the pinned repo map's language, and SHALL raise for an unmapped repo without a `language` column; WHEN `external.resolve_task` gets a cached instance ID THE SYSTEM SHALL return its `ExternalTask` only when `admit` says admitted, and SHALL return `None` for a refused or unknown name; WHEN `run.py --tasks` names an admitted instance ID THE SYSTEM SHALL register it in `TASKS` and run its cell through `prepare`, and `--tasks all` SHALL plan no external cell; THE FeatureBench candidate set SHALL hold only `.lv1` IDs and exclude the deferred heavy-environment repositories; WHEN the preflight CLI runs with no arguments THE SYSTEM SHALL try a SWE-bench Multilingual fallback only after its primary pick is refused, report `featurebench_admitted`, `go_admitted`, and `rust_admitted`, and exit nonzero naming the empty family when any one of them is 0, else exit 0; WHEN it runs with `--panel PATH` THE SYSTEM SHALL admit exactly the panel's FeatureBench and SWE-bench Multilingual members and exit nonzero naming any refused member or when no FeatureBench member is admitted, else exit 0.  (G-1, G-3, F-1)
- AC-6: WHEN `run.py` writes any row, local or external, including failure rows and reused stored rows, THE SYSTEM SHALL include `contaminated` as a bool; WHEN the row has a trajectory sidecar THE SYSTEM SHALL scan its tool-call inputs, and WHEN an input reads a path under the tilth `benchmark/` tree or the harness data directory or fetches the task's upstream repository or package source THE SYSTEM SHALL record `contaminated: true` and the hits; WHEN no input matches THE SYSTEM SHALL record `contaminated: false`; WHEN no sidecar exists THE SYSTEM SHALL record `contaminated: true` with an `unscanned` hit; and in every case THE SYSTEM SHALL leave `correct` equal to the grader verdict.  (F-1, G-1, G-3)

